## Goal
Address review feedback on the sync feature: make file copying atomic and fix iCloud path detection. The session slice was empty, so this is inferred from the commit message alone.

## Problems
- Copying directly to the destination can leave a partial or corrupt file if the process is interrupted.
- iCloud detection matched without requiring a path separator, so similar-looking paths could be misidentified as iCloud locations (a false positive).

## Decision
- Copy to a temporary file in the destination directory, then rename it over the target. A rename on the same filesystem is atomic, so readers see either the old file or the complete new one.
- Require a path separator in the iCloud check so only real path components match, not arbitrary substrings.
- Both changes follow code review comments.

